 ## Background
-Originated in the paper "Implicit Geometric Regularization for Learning Shapes" [S1, unofficial]. The analysis is presented as Theorem 1 and Theorem 2, justifying the use of the Eikonal regularization term alone for implicitly regularizing the zero level set. It contrasts with previous works that used Eikonal regularization in combination with other explicit reconstruction terms. The analysis uses perturbation theory for eigenvalues and eigenvectors of Hermitian matrices [S1, unofficial].
